Z||000003||2birds||02-05-2000||09:32 PM||||My ST's don't move at all.  They fit in the pockets real nice.  How's the ride with the Eibachs?||||reg||1
Z||000004||FIEROCIOUS||02-06-2000||11:59 AM||||The Eibachs came <A HREF="http://www.SHOX.com" TARGET=_blank>www.SHOX.com</A>  if you have a buisness license you can get them at cost 200.00, ST are 167.00. Also The Eibachs were ruff on hard bumps but after a day or so either I'm getting used to them or the 300lbs of tools in the back made it ride ruff go fig? I highly recomend them for Auto cross MAN IT STICKS, BIG improvement!||||reg||1
Z||000005||FIEROCIOUS||02-20-2000||02:50 AM||||Low Fiero owners I would like to hear from you all! I don't know of many fieros with Eibachs. Any body else useing them? Does any one know the spring rates of the S/T's? Or the Eibachs? <BR>Please help a Fiero Brother out!||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||02-21-2000||11:30 AM||||I have an Eibach Pro-Kit! Love them! Had a problem with the rear driverside spring poping out and being loud and annoying.. I took the rubber insulator on the top out and they don't move anymore... Unless its on the lift at the shop.. then you have to hold them in place while you lower the car... not as much of a pain as it may sound. NEVER have a problem with the front. Their riding on Konis. Love the ride. According to the Eibach Literature their Pro-kit springs are 35% stiffer. (Not sure if that helps but if you know the factory spring rate.. well just add 35% to it... )||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||02-22-2000||05:38 PM||||I've driven two Fiero's (85GT/86SE)with Eibachs and found them to be way too stiff with the KYB's. They were fine on perfectly flat road, but you could feel every ant you smashed. I have Eibach/KYB's in my Ciera GT. They are stiffer but not a busy as the they are in the Fiero.<P>Has anyone been able to compare them directly to ST's? Kinda' curious.||||reg||13
